# U-Boot default environment for the OnePlus Nord N100, used instead of
# U-Boot's board/qualcomm/qcom-phone.env (which it is based on).
#
# Why: the mainline billie2 device tree doesn't describe the volume keys, and
# the power key doesn't reach U-Boot either (tested 2026-11-20), so the
# button-driven boot menu can't be used. Instead, if there's nothing to boot,
# U-Boot goes straight into USB fastboot. From the host:
#   fastboot oem console          read everything U-Boot printed
#   fastboot oem run:<command>    run a U-Boot command (FASTBOOT_OEM_RUN)
#   fastboot reboot               leave

bootdelay=0
stdin=serial,button-kbd
stdout=serial,vidconsole
stderr=serial,vidconsole

# Fastboot is keen to use the address from kconfig, but we allocate its buffer
# at runtime.
fastboot=fastboot -l $fastboot_addr_r usb 0

# Probe UFS before anything else (board code should do it too).
preboot=scsi scan

# Try the normal EFI boot (GRUB on the ESP); if that returns, stay reachable
# over USB instead of waiting for a key press nobody can make.
bootcmd=bootefi bootmgr; echo "No bootable OS, entering USB fastboot"; run fastboot
